(1) A person shall qualify to act as a trustee if that person—
  (a) is above the age of eighteen years;
  (b) is not disqualified under any other written law from appointment as such; and
  (c) meets any other requirement as may be prescribed in the Regulations or any other written law.
(2) A person shall be disqualified for appointment as a trustee if that person—
  (a) is disqualified from acting as a director or secretary of a company in accordance with the Companies Act;
  (b) is disqualified from acting as a liquidator or administrator under the Insolvency Act;
  (c) has been declared mentally incapacitated under the Mental Health Act;
  (d) has been convicted of a criminal offence which attracts imprisonment for a term exceeding six months;
  (e) has been convicted of corruption or an economic crime; or Property acquired illegally. Cap. 59A.
