48.text:
(1) Every trustee shall keep adequate, accurate, Duty to keep and up-to-date records of the trust and all matters relating records. to the administration of the trust.
(2) The information referred to in the records shall include—
  (a) the information relating to the settlor, each trustee including foreign trustees if any, each enforcer, 576 Trust Administration each beneficiary, and each beneficial owner as prescribed in the Regulations;
  (b) information relating to a trust agent of the trust;
  (c) the trust deed and any other documents that contain terms of the trust;
  (d) the certificate of registration or incorporation;
  (e) any amendment of a trust deed and details of its effect on the trust property;
  (f) records of the trust property that identify the assets, liabilities, income and expenses relating to the trust property and beneficial ownership of the trust property;
  (g) any foreign trust administered by the trustees, including—
  (i) details of the foreign trust such as the settlors, trustees, beneficiaries, protectors or enforcers, if any;
  (ii) information on the beneficial owners of the foreign trust;
  (iii) property of the trust within Kenya; and
  (iv) records of transactions that have any connection with Kenya;
  (h) all transactions, advisory communications and matters relating to trust accounts including trust investments;
  (i) prescribed details relating to financial institutions and reporting institutions—
  (i) with which the trust has business relationships with and the nature of that business relationship;
  (ii) which the trust uses as agents to perform any of the trustee’s functions relating to the trust property; and
  (iii) from which the trust obtains any services in respect of the trustee’s functions relating to the trust property;
  (j) any written contracts entered into during the tenure of the trustee;
  (k) any records of resolutions of the trustees made during tenure of the trustee;
  (l) any management records and books of accounts prepared during the tenure of the trustee;
  (m) documents of appointment, removal and discharge of trustees, including any court orders appointing or removing trustees;
  (n) any reports of material irregularities and how the trustee dealt with those material irregularities;
  (o) a register of charges and security rights created under the Movable Property Security Rights Act or Cap. 499A. any other law; and
  (p) any other document necessary for the administration of the trust.
(3) The trustees shall ensure that the records are kept for at least seven years from—
  (a) the date of termination or dissolution of the trust; or
  (b) the date they cease being trustees of a trust.
(4) A trustee shall lodge with the Registrar a copy of any amendment to the trust deed or the list of assets within twenty-one days after making the amendment:
Provided that a trustee shall obtain any approval required under any other written law prior to lodging the amendment.
(5) A trustee who fails to comply with subsection (4) shall be liable to an administrative penalty of—
  (a) seven thousand shillings, if the trustee in default is a natural person; and
  (b) fourteen thousand shillings, if the trustee in default is a body corporate.

